From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:39:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: support firmware 1.9.1 and 1.9.2

Rework the AS21xxx PHY driver for operation with Aeonsemi firmware
1.9.1 and 1.9.2. Probe the running firmware version, use the shared
mailbox and copper-autonegotiation ABI for both releases, and issue
the newer LED, counter and SerDes reset operations only when 1.9.2
support is detected. Unknown versions retain the 1.9.1-compatible
feature subset so an unsupported command cannot desynchronise the
mailbox.

The rework also adds parity synchronisation, firmware check-and-load
via firmware-name, MDI/MDI-X control, master/slave configuration,
downshift and fast-retrain tunables, PHY statistics, cable diagnostics,
USXGMII in-band host-ready handling, LED hardware control mapping and a
gen1/gen2 probe split.

The proprietary vendor BBU API and debugfs interface are not included.
The driver uses a self-contained, mutex-serialized mailbox implementation
and builds with the upstream single-object Makefile rule.

Note: this replaces large parts of the current in-tree driver; for a
kernel submission it should be split into incremental changes.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
