+/* AS21xxx ID Legend
+ * AS21x1xxB1
+ *     ^ ^^
+ *     | |J: Supports SyncE/PTP
+ *     | |P: No SyncE/PTP support
+ *     | 1: Supports 2nd Serdes
+ *     | 0: No 2nd SerDes support
+ *     0: 10G, 5G, 2.5G
+ *     5: 5G, 2.5G
+ *     2: 2.5G
+ *
+ * The varying model digit is encoded in PHY ID bits 7:4. Bits 7:6 select
+ * the speed grade, bit 5 distinguishes the one/two-SerDes 10G and 5G
+ * variants, and bit 4 distinguishes J from P. The 2.5G family only has a
+ * single-SerDes variant, so bit 5 is not an independent capability bit for
+ * that speed grade. Bits 3:0 are the standard PHY revision field; revision
+ * value 2 is sold as B1. The fixed "1" after the speed digit is product
+ * nomenclature and is not represented by a separate ID field.
+ */
